  "body": "**Negative result (no \u03ba claim).** This builds and prices an actual legal owner fill for the [#2339](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2339) 80-alias T74 words. It also certifies a width-aware ceiling for every such fill. Both lie **below** #2269, so the low-alias inventory is cost-negative on the unchanged T74 template.\n\n| object | b |\n|---|---|\n| #2339's estimate (width-blind cap \u00d7 #2269's realized fraction) | \u2248 0.0017259 (**wrong**) |\n| width-blind R = 48 cap (merged `complex-local-word-ceiling`) | 0.0017479583719744 |\n| **certified width-aware ceiling, any legal whole-helper fill** | **< 0.0016867** |\n| **realized legal fill OWNERS-80** (native, bracket width 1e-40) | **0.00168654323626906426826\u2026** |\n| #2269 claimed b | 0.00169624713905847422\u2026 |\n\n**What was learned.** The low aliases free 121 local rank units per call. But they swap width-8 helpers, which pack exactly into the rank-8/16/32 bins, for width-9 lenders. In the LP optimum, 27,824 rank-32 bins then host [9,9,9] and keep a rank-5 idle child, and 6,068 rank-16 bins host a lone [9] and keep a rank-7 child. That fragmentation costs more than the freed mass.\n\nThe fill realizes **99.994%** of its ceiling, so better packing cannot rescue it. The \"+5 high aliases\" give **exactly zero** gain: each one turns a local rank-5 child into an idle rank-5 remainder, and the ceiling equals #2269's to all digits. Positive controls: #2269 realizes 99.991% of its own ceiling (b < 0.0016965), and #2322 realizes 99.992% (b < 0.0016973). Neither is rejected at its claim.\n\n**Overlap.** [#2360](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2360) (Jeremy Diviney) independently certifies b < 0.0016870 for the same words with the same 1,163-pattern relaxation; it appeared while this was in progress. This PR adds:\n- the **attainable side**: a legal 266,400-role fill, independently recounted;\n- a tighter certificate from the real 249/417 dispatch (b < 0.0016867 vs < 0.0016870);\n- the variant and control cases;\n- an **independent re-check of #2360's `DUAL.json`**: 1,163/1,163 inequalities hold, the lower bound of 66304\u00b7mu is 66304.0043 under its envelope, and a tampered dual is rejected.\n\nThe relaxation method comes from #1129 (Ali Romman) and the R480 pattern-dual audit.\n\n**Checks.**\n- `fill_check80.py` is standalone, adapted from our #2315 checker. It recounts OWNERS-80 against the pinned #2339 words and the #2269 GLOBAL-TEMPLATE under rules R-a..R-g:\n  - widths and one role per helper;\n  - capacity and prefix-filled slices;\n  - idle and profile recount;\n  - roles strictly inside rebuilt windows;\n  - families: owner\u00b7896 + (2\u00b7pair+side)\u00b7112 + port, never the caller's active pair;\n  - #2322's private namespace (physical 66714, 44 buffers in reserve);\n  - X2 pending-axis disjointness and 3,175 73-column charts.\n- It rejects **16 mutations** and accepts #2269's own fill as a positive control.\n- `price80.py` gives the 1e-40 native and conservative brackets, with 12 controls; the fill is rejected at #2269's b and at #2322's \u03ba.\n\n**Reproduce** (standard library only; `--fetch` pulls `refs/pull/2269/head` b479fc55 and `refs/pull/2322/head` 002304ef if absent):\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-80alias-owner-fill/run_all.py --fetch   # ~25 s -> PASS_T74_80ALIAS_RUN_ALL roles=266400 ... below_2269=1 below_2322=1\npython3 -I -B research/t74-80alias-owner-fill/ceiling_lp.py        # ~7 s  -> PASS_T74_WIDTH_AWARE_CEILING\n```\nThe #2339 words come from commit bf1742ae when present, otherwise from blob- and sha256-pinned copies in `inputs/`. The rebuild (`build_fill.py`, about 230 s, deterministic) is optional.\n\n**Pins.**\n- Base: canonical main `0fdd7d82`.\n- Task card: `complex-new-helper-inventory`, scope refined to this inventory.\n- Package metadata (`--check-only`) passes; 65/65 research tests pass (2 skipped).\n\n**Environment.** Everything was run on CPython 3.14.4 (Linux), plus a 3.10 grammar check. The registered 3.12 replay was not run locally because 3.12 is unavailable here.\n\n**Scope.** This is a finite fill plus a scoped relaxation ceiling for the fixed #2339 words, unsplit helpers and the unchanged #2269 bin stock. It is not an impossibility result for partial alias subsets, a changed bin stock, split reservations or a changed local contract; these are listed as open next questions. Native lowering of the 64 initial corrections and 37 warps, lender lifetimes, X-field ownership, buffers, prefix bits, the PLAN/SPEC refreeze and the outer ledger remain unchecked. They cannot help, because the fill already loses. The selected frontier is untouched.\n\n**Credits.**\n- #2339 (this author).\n- #2269 Jeremy Kothe.\n- #2322 Vlado Vojdanovski.\n- #2312 / #2302 jeremykothe2.\n- #2226 Cinna Davis.\n- #1319 / #1297 T74 lineage (Rohan Arun et al.).\n- Douglas Colkitt's cap model.\n- #2360 Jeremy Diviney (concurrent; `DUAL.json` copied byte-for-byte).\n- #1129 Ali Romman.\n- #2374 / #2349 / #2363 are cited as reference points.\n\nPrepared with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5). An AI subagent reviewed the fill checker; no independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
